{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And if he is not redeemed by these.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in the first chapter of Qiddushin: 'or his uncle' — this is redemption by relatives; 'or his hand has attained' — this is redemption by himself; 'and he shall be redeemed' — this is redemption by others. Therefore it says, ״ואם לא יגאל ויצא בשנת היובל״ — against the will of the gentile, for the verse speaks of a gentile who is under your hand, as is taught there in the Gemara: concerning a gentile who is not under your hand, what can one do to him? And there they interpreted: just as redemption by himself is for release, so redemption by his relatives is for release; and just as redemption by himself is for release, so redemption by others is for release. And thus they concluded at the end and said: the verse is interpreted both from what precedes it and from what follows it, and all is for release."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:31.341579161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}